    simple_audio_cuda_q15_intermittent_device_failure_2026_11_26, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Q15 CUDA audio spec fails intermittently on the device", src/runtime/sffi/simple_audio_cuda_driver.c, 125, test/03_system/io_audio/simple_audio_cuda_q15_env_spec.spl, 2026-11-26, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    simple_audio_cuda_q15_intermittent_device_failure_2026_11_26, 0, "2026-11-26 NVIDIA GB10 aarch64, seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-claude-cudagated-1126/release/simple: 7 runs, 4 pass (readback samples 16384 16384 0 -2048 as asserted), 2 cuda-audio-readback-failed, 1 cuda-audio-module-load-failed. Other sessions shared the GPU during the runs."
    simple_audio_cuda_q15_intermittent_device_failure_2026_11_26, 1, "2026-11-27 fix implemented (release/1.0.0 7ec0a1ed579, work/w7-3-p2-backlog-triage-and-fixes-20261127): updated src/runtime/sffi/simple_audio_cuda_driver.c to resolve cuCtxSetCurrent and re-bind d->context via ensure_context(d) before every CUDA driver call (module_load, module_unload, alloc, free, upload, download, launch, sync, close), clear d->context=NULL on close, and capture driver CUresult into d->last_error (keeping the 13-symbol SFFI ABI unchanged). Verified C syntax on Windows via clang.exe -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra (exit 0 with scratch POSIX header stubs) and ran Windows interpreter audio specs: simple_audio_cuda_q15_packed_bounds_spec 3/3 PASS, simple_audio_cuda_q15_env_spec 1/1 PASS (env_skip: CUDA absent on Windows), simple_audio_contract_spec 4/4 PASS, simple_audio_device_spec 4/4 PASS, simple_audio_offload_spec 5/5 PASS, simple_audio_period_ring_spec 3/3 PASS. Status=fix-implemented-verification-pending: requires Linux + NVIDIA GPU rebuild of libsimple_audio_cuda.so via scripts/build/build_simple_audio_cuda_sffi.shs and repeated SIMPLE_CUDA_TEST=1 runs of test/03_system/io_audio/simple_audio_cuda_q15_env_spec.spl."

